          "label": "<p>The rootlets of the hypoglossal nerve (CN XII) emerge from the medulla between w</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>The rootlets of the hypoglossal nerve (CN XII) emerge from the medulla between which two surface landmarks?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Gracile tubercle and cuneate tubercle</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>These are posterior surface landmarks overlying the dorsal column nuclei. CN XII rootlets emerge from the anterior surface, not the posterior.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Pyramid and olive</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. CN XII rootlets exit in the anterolateral sulcus between the pyramid (medial) and olive (lateral) — a key identification point in neuroanatomy dissections.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Olive and inferior cerebellar peduncle</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>The rootlets of CN IX, X, and XI emerge lateral to the olive — not CN XII, which exits medial to the olive.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Anterior median fissure and pyramid</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>No cranial nerve rootlets emerge from the anterior median fissure. CN XII exits between the pyramid and the olive, lateral to the fissure.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "Review the anterior surface: pyramids lie medially flanking the fissure, olives lie laterally, and CN XII rootlets exit between them. CN IX, X, and XI emerge lateral to the olive."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Well done. Remembering that CN XII lies between the pyramid and olive helps you locate both the nerve and the two most prominent anterior landmarks in one relationship."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
